# Patient data — never committed
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf.gz.tbi
*.bam
*.cram
*.fastq*
*.fq.gz
*.docx
gated-data/
work/
# Secrets / sessions / screenshots
*token*
.userdata-*
shots/
*.png
# ...except the one generated figure the PDF build needs. `*.png` above exists to keep
# screenshots out, because a screenshot can contain anything that was on the screen. The
# mechanism figure is generated from docs/mechanism_graph.yaml and contains no patient
# data, and make_pdf.sh reads the PNG specifically -- without it a fresh clone cannot
# build the submission PDF, and step 15 cannot regenerate it because that step stats the
# controlled area. Narrow exception rather than dropping the rule.
!docs/figures/mechanism.png
# Env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Track 2 Spec 1: private files with coordinates (second guard; they live outside the repo anyway)
config/local.env
handoff_from_track1.yaml
transcript_facts.yaml
t2_variants.*

# Working registers and run outputs live outside the repo; guard in case they are copied in
# (registers/evidence_ledger.csv carries genomic coordinates and must never be committed).
registers/
results/
# Superseded drafts, superseded by docs/REPORT.md and docs/PITCH.md
docs/REPORT_v2.md
docs/PITCH_v2.md

# Per-tool local operating notes. CLAUDE.md is committed because reviewers should see the
# data-handling tiers the work actually ran under; AGENTS.md is the same file mechanically
# rewritten for a second tool and is NOT a deliverable. The reviewed AI disclosure is
# docs/METHODS_AND_AI.md, evidenced by registers/ai_usage_register.csv.
AGENTS.md

# docs/PITCH_STORYBOARD.md — how to record the pitch (slide plan, what must not appear on
# camera, upload order). A production aid, not a submission deliverable: PITCH.md is the
# script of record and the manifest gates it. Kept local for the same reason as AGENTS.md.
docs/PITCH_STORYBOARD.md

# Pitch deck (production aid, like PITCH_STORYBOARD.md): not a submission deliverable.
docs/pitch_deck.*
docs/pitch_deck.pdf

# BUILDER_TASKS_<date>.md — the internal work order for a build session (what to verify, what to
# commit, what not to read). Same class as AGENTS.md and PITCH_STORYBOARD.md: a production aid, not
# a deliverable, and it ages badly — the 2026-10-19 sheet still said "expect 12 PASS" when the
# engine had 28 self-tests, and it carried an instruction to reword a data-handling caveat that
# docs/METHODS_AND_AI.md is the record for. Kept local.
BUILDER_TASKS_*.md
